// Proofs for the identities identities.hana states, in the strategy
// language of docs/proving.md. An identity with no entry here is proved by
// `diagram` alone — this file holds exactly the claims that need direction.

// The right-hand side is written as the call it is, and the engine is not
// allowed to spend a sentence's definition on its own: say so.
proof identities::testing_a_test_by_name = inline diagram;

// The arm recomputes the very test its branch decided. The driver
// identifies the two computations — `view-value`, then `dedup` — and the
// case split on the one wire that remains decides both readings at once:
// η, spent deliberately, where no rewrite window could.
proof identities::specializing_a_tested_value = both(decide) cases(equal);
